// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// W2 · THE SEED DUMP — the founder's constants, printed as SQL, once.
//
// `docs/sql/w2-seed-founder.sql` is GENERATED by this test from the live Swift
// constants (`Program.all`, `Phases.all`, `Levers.all` + `.schedule`,
// `Programs.cutTargets` / `.bulkTargets`, `PhaseGoals`, `PrTruth.floor(for:)`,
// `Supplements.protocolSeed`) so that not one number in the seed is typed by
// hand. Parity is by construction: the rows ARE the constants.
//
// The exercise uuids come from the founder's live catalogue, captured by the
// schema-truth-checker on 2026-09-10 and pinned below; the payload resolves
// each program movement through `ExerciseIndex` — the same exact-then-
// normalised rule the sync uses — so the routine row names the catalogue row
// the phone already files that movement's sets under.
//
// One-off: it writes only when `ONYX_SEED_OUT` names a file, and the
// constants it reads are deleted at the end of W2, taking this test with
// them. What it asserts without the env var is the part that must stay true
// of the file already checked in: every statement is scoped to the founder,
// and the second account gets nothing.
//
//   ONYX_SEED_OUT=docs/sql/w2-seed-founder.sql \
//   ONYX_TEMPLATES_OUT=native/Onyx/Resources/plan-templates.json \
//   npm run swift:data -- --filter SeedDumpTests
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

